Engine (engine/)
  DOSBox, by the DOSBox Team (https://www.dosbox.com), SVN r4305, as ported
  to Emscripten by Boris Gjenero as em-dosbox
  (https://github.com/dreamlayers/em-dosbox, branch em-dosbox-svn-sdl2,
  commit e1f72dd11513c9ddc6e2a9c1f08ff50581c320f7, 2023-01-06).
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 (engine/COPYING).

  This is a modified version of the program. frunk.store's changes for the
  browser are in engine/em-dosbox-web.patch (also
  tools/elderscrolls/em-dosbox-web.patch in
  https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose
  tools/build-elderscrolls.mjs builds it with Emscripten 4.0.10), each
  change marked "[frunk]". The complete patched source the build came from
  is engine/em-dosbox-e1f72dd-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: linked as an ES module with JSPI in place of Asyncify, so
  DOSBox's own loop and its file reads can wait for the page; it lets the
  page run through a MessageChannel message rather than a timer, and uses
  up to 90% of the CPU rather than 60%; no splash screen and no DOSBox
  hotkeys; the page can type keys and read how many frames were drawn and
  where the game has the mouse pointer; and the pointer goes where it is
  on the screen even when a game narrows the mouse's range (Daggerfall's
  was about 5% short). Built without em-dosbox's function-array CPU cores,
  which are slower in WebAssembly.

  Libraries compiled into it: Emscripten's SDL2 port (zlib license);
  Emscripten itself (MIT / University of Illinois/NCSA licenses).

Games (data/)
  The Elder Scrolls: Arena Copyright 1994 Bethesda Softworks, and The Elder
  Scrolls II: Daggerfall Copyright 1996 Bethesda Softworks. Bethesda made
  both freeware, Arena in 2004 and Daggerfall in 2009, from its own server
  (https://cdnstatic.bethsoft.com/elderscrolls.com/assets/files/tes/extras/):
    Arena106Setup.zip  sha256 aed6d15d9cd29fde12464097fd73e0c9fa290d2a57979e84a1cc8ac0c3fb1fc7
    DFInstall.zip      sha256 a9ba539d56f84f28b9da8c0a1d5ef5d34ccd6dcb5003f2bb2f5aa8baf6ffe828
  Bethesda's terms and setup notes that came with them are
  data/arena-setup.pdf and data/daggerfall-legal.pdf.

  tools/build-elderscrolls.mjs takes the files out:
    Arena: the ARENA folder from Arena106.exe (a RAR self-extractor inside
    the zip), unchanged.
    Daggerfall: the DAGGER folder from the zip's DFCD (the CD), set up as
    its installer's "huge" install would: ARCH3D.BSA and DAGGER.SND
    unpacked from PACKED.DAT (which isn't kept), Bethesda's 1.07.213 patch
    (DAG213.EXE, from the same zip) applied by running it in DOSBox, and
    the installer's Z.CFG and HMISET.CFG (Sound Blaster 16) written.
  For downloading, each game's files are stored one after another in 1 MB
  pieces (data/arena/, data/daggerfall/; some gzipped), which the page
  joins back into the same files.
